      "source_key": "jtwc_abpw|western_north_pacific_area|invest_94w",
      "content_hash": "bde0a6b4f3ceae6a",
      "platform_summary": "8.3N 167.4E | winds 18-23 kt | 1008 mb | MEDIUM",
      "platform_location": "8.3N 167.4E",
      "wind": "18-23 kt",
      "risk_48h": null,
      "risk_7d": null,
      "next_update": null,
      "raw_text": "(1) THE AREA OF CONVECTION (INVEST 94W) PREVIOUSLY LOCATED \nNEAR 8.1N 167.9E IS NOW LOCATED NEAR 8.3N 167.4E, APPROXIMATELY \n47 NM SOUTHWEST OF KWAJALEIN. ANIMATED ENHANCED INFRARED (EIR) \nSATELLITE IMAGERY DEPICTS 94W WITH A CONSOLIDATING LOW-LEVEL \nCIRCULATION CENTER THAT HAS TUCKED UNDERNEATH THE SOUTHEASTERN \nQUADRANT OF PERSISTENT CONVECTION. A 030910Z ASCAT-B PASS REVEALED \nA BAND OF 15-20 KNOT WINDS WRAPPING AROUND THE NORTHEN PERIPHERY OF \nTHE CIRCULATION. ENVIRONMENTAL ANALYSIS REVEALS MARGINALLY FAVORABLE \nCONDITIONS FOR DEVELOPMENT WITH LOW TO MODERATE VERTICAL WIND SHEAR \n(15-20 KTS), WEAK EQUATORWARD OUTFLOW ALOFT, AND WARM (29-30 C) SEA \nSURFACE TEMPERATURES. GLOBAL MODELS ARE IN FAIR AGREEMENT THAT 94W \nWILL BE QUASI-STATIONARY OVER THE NEXT 24 HOURS AS IT CONTINUES TO \nCONSOLIDATE. MAXIMUM SUSTAINED SURFACE WINDS ARE ESTIMATED AT 18 \nTO 23 KNOTS. MINIMUM SEA LEVEL PRESSURE IS ESTIMATED TO BE NEAR \n1008 MB. THE POTENTIAL FOR THE DEVELOPMENT OF A SIGNIFICANT \nTROPICAL CYCLONE WITHIN THE NEXT 24 HOURS IS UPGRADED TO MEDIUM.",
      "metadata": {
        "basin_section": "WESTERN NORTH PACIFIC AREA (180 TO MALAY PENINSULA)",
        "invest_id": "94W",
